// ⛔ DO NOT DEPLOY THIS WORKER WITHOUT READING THIS BLOCK FIRST (WIC-2109 / WIC-2108).
//
// SUPERSEDED BY THE PAGES PATH. The three hostnames below are already served by the
// `careerpin-marketing` Cloudflare Pages project, re-asserted by CI on every marketing
// deploy (`.github/workflows/deploy-marketing.yml`):
//
//   * `:112-114` — CNAME upserts pointing `www.careerpin.app`, `careerpin.io` and
//     `www.careerpin.io` at `careerpin-marketing.pages.dev`, all `proxied: true`.
//     (`:110` does the same for the `careerpin.app` apex, which is the redirect target,
//     not a redirect surface.)
//   * `:156` "Add redirect custom domains to Pages project" — `add_domain` for the same
//     three hostnames at `:178-180`.
//   * The redirect itself is `packages/marketing/_worker.js`, a Pages advanced-mode
//     worker: it serves assets for the `careerpin.app` apex and 301s every other
//     hostname to it. `packages/marketing/_redirects` carries the same three rules as
//     a belt-and-braces fallback. `deploy-marketing.yml:136` publishes
//     `packages/marketing`, so both ship on every marketing deploy.
//
// ⚠️ CORRECTION (WIC-2111). The previous revision of this block cited
// `packages/infra/redirect-pages/_redirects` as the mechanism. That is WRONG, and it is
// worth knowing why: `packages/infra/redirect-pages/` IS DEPLOYED BY NOTHING. The only
// `pages deploy` anywhere in this repo targets `packages/marketing` — grep for it. That
// sibling directory is a second orphan sitting next to this one, not the live path.
//
// So DEPLOYING THIS WORKER WOULD CONTEST ROUTES CI ASSIGNS TO A PAGES PROJECT. A Worker
// route and a Pages custom domain on the same hostname are two systems claiming one name;
// whichever ran last wins, and the next marketing deploy re-asserts the Pages side.
//
// ⛔ DO NOT TRY TO SETTLE THIS WITH `curl`. The redirect expression in
// `packages/marketing/_worker.js` is BYTE-IDENTICAL to `worker.js` in this directory —
// both build `https://careerpin.app${url.pathname}${url.search}` and hand it to
// `Response.redirect(…, 301)`. Measured live 2026-09-05: all three hostnames 301 to the
// apex with path and query preserved, and `careerpin.app` itself serves the site (200).
// That is exactly what BOTH implementations predict, so the HTTP surface cannot tell you
// which one served it. No external probe ever will.
//
// Before running `wrangler deploy` here, confirm (a) whether the `careerpin-redirects`
// Worker exists at all, and (b) whether it holds routes on those three hostnames. No
// agent seat holds a Cloudflare credential — but CI does. Dispatch
// `.github/workflows/careerpin-redirect-ownership-probe.yml`, which answers both from
// the Cloudflare control plane with read-only GETs, rather than opening the dashboard.
// Until that has been run, do not assume this Worker was deployed, and do not assume it
// was not.
//
// WHY THIS FILE IS `.jsonc` AND NOT `.toml` (WIC-2107 / WIC-2109). Wrangler resolves its
// config with three independent find-up walks, one per filename, in the order
// `wrangler.json` -> `wrangler.jsonc` -> `wrangler.toml`. FILENAME PRECEDENCE IS EVALUATED
// BEFORE DIRECTORY PROXIMITY, so while this file was `wrangler.toml` the repo-root
// `wrangler.jsonc` won the `.jsonc` pass before the `.toml` pass ever started:
// `cd packages/infra/redirect-worker && npx wrangler deploy` silently deployed the
// PRODUCTION `jobtrail` app instead of this Worker. As `.jsonc` it wins its own directory
// by proximity. `scripts/wrangler-config-resolution-check.py` (Check B) guards this.
// Renaming it back to `.toml` re-arms that footgun.
{
	"name": "careerpin-redirects",
	"main": "worker.js",
	"compatibility_date": "2026-06-09",

	// Routes: bind this worker to www.careerpin.app, careerpin.io, and www.careerpin.io.
	// All three 301 → https://careerpin.app (apex).
	// careerpin.com is intentionally NOT a route — it is held by a 2018 squatter and is not owned.
	// Domains registered 2026-06-11 (WIC-506 done). Each hostname needs a proxied DNS record in its
	// Cloudflare zone before this worker route activates (see WIC-522 DNS plan document).
	"routes": [
		{ "pattern": "www.careerpin.app/*", "zone_id": "ace9c419c6a5129cf7b8d104528a29e1" },
		{ "pattern": "careerpin.io/*", "zone_id": "e31283e2f9ddc738087daaf4698fb88c" },
		{ "pattern": "www.careerpin.io/*", "zone_id": "e31283e2f9ddc738087daaf4698fb88c" }
	]
}
